umented report and notification API operations.\",\n  \"Push-notification delivery and automatic release-time scheduling beyond documented contract operations.\",\n  \"Parking policies and external workflows not explicitly defined by `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n  \"Database migration, legacy-data backfill, and preservation of pre-existing App database contents; this implementation assumes a fresh database and uses startup `EnsureCreated`.\",\n  \"Web or mobile employee-facing product screens are excluded from this API-repository change.\"\n ],\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"OAuth client ID and redirect URI are configured for deployment.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains an `authorizationUrl` reflecting the configured client ID and redirect URI and a non-empty `state`.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Required Google OAuth configuration or authorization service is unavailable.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 503 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a client requests `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement `getGoogleAuthorization` according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`, constructing the Google Workspace authorization URL from deployment-configured OAuth values.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid Google Workspace authorization code and matching state identify an eligible Folio3 employee.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n  