mail`, `dedicatedParking`, `assignedFloor`, `assignedSpace`, and the employee's `vehicles` list.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/employees/me`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The bearer token is absent or invalid, the identity lacks access, or no employee profile exists.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401, 403, or 404 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/employees/me`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/employees/me`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getMyEmployeeProfile` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session and available App database identify an employee.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response dashboard contains the contract's required fields, including `officeDate`, `timezone`, `releaseTime`, `assignedSpace`, `spaceStatus`, `availableSpaces`, `registeredVehicle`, `workingDays`, and `workingDayRule`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/dashboard`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/dashboard`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/dashboard`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getParkingDashboard` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The bearer session identifies an employee with dedicated parking and the submitted `officeDate` is today in the office timezone and releasable.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response release contains `officeDate`, `space`, `status`, `claimableAt`, and `auditEvents`, including a `Released` action.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee posts the today-release request.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated, the employee is not eligible to release dedicated parking, or the release conflicts with the current parking state.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401, 403, or 409 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/parking/releases/today`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/parking/releases/today`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `releaseTodaysSpace` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with registered vehicles.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response `vehicles` list contains only that employee's vehicles with contract fields, including `id`, `plate`, `make`, `model`, `color`, and `active`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/vehicles`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/vehicles`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/vehicles`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `listMyVehicles` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session and vehicle input with a valid plate and optional make, model, and color are supplied.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response vehicle record contains `id`, `plate`, `make`, `model`, `color`, and `active` set to true.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee posts the vehicle input to `/api/vehicles`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The vehicle input is invalid, the request is unauthenticated, or the plate conflicts with an existing record.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 401, or 409 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/vehicles`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/vehicles`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `registerVehicle` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with saved releases and audit events.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response `releases` list contains only that employee's releases with contract fields, including `id`, `officeDate`, `space`, `status`, `claimableAt`, and `auditEvents`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/releases`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/releases`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/releases`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `listMyReleases` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies a dedicated-parking holder and `officeDates` contains one or more valid dates within the next 30 calendar days.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response `releases` list contains the saved dates and a `Scheduled` audit event for each release.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee posts the schedule to `/api/parking/releases`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The schedule request is malformed, the employee is not eligible, or dates violate the contract's date rules.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 403, or 422 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/parking/releases`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/parking/releases`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `scheduleParkingReleases` operation for one or more dates within the next 30 calendar days according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The bearer session owns an unclaimed scheduled release identified by `releaseId`.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200, the response release status is `Cancelled`, and its `auditEvents` list includes scheduling and cancellation events.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee deletes `/api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The release does not exist, belongs to another employee, has already been claimed, or the request is unauthenticated.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 404, 403, 409, or 401 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client deletes `/api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `DELETE /api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `cancelParkingRelease` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session exists and office capacity, release time, and current parking allocations are configured.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains `officeDate`, `timezone`, `availableSpaces`, `releaseTime`, and a `floors` list with `floor`, `freeSpaces`, and `totalSpaces`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/availability`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/availability`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/availability`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getParkingAvailability` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an eligible employee, the selected registered vehicle belongs to that employee, and a space is claimable for `officeDate`.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response contains allocated `floor`, `space`, `plate`, `officeDate`, `status`, `entryStatus`, `floorCapacity`, `allocationRule`, and `authorizationScope` fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee posts `vehicleId` and `officeDate` to `/api/parking/claims`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Two eligible employees attempt to claim the last available space for the same office date concurrently.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The responses contain exactly one status 201 and one conflict status 409, and the successful response contains one allocated space.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employees submit claims concurrently.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is invalid or unauthenticated, the employee is ineligible, the vehicle or date is not eligible, or no space remains available.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 401, 403, 409, or 422 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/parking/claims`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/parking/claims`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `claimParkingSpace` operation, allocating a claimable temporary space using the submitted registered vehicle, according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with an active temporary allocation for today.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the allocation's required `ParkingClaim` fields, including `floor`, `space`, `plate`, `officeDate`, and `entryStatus`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/claims/today`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The employee has no temporary allocation for today or the request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 404 or 401 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values when an error response is returned.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/claims/today`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/claims/today`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getTodaysParkingClaim` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The bearer session owns an existing claim that can be cancelled.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the contract's `ParkingClaim` fields, including `id` and the cancellation outcome status.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee deletes `/api/parking/claims/{claimId}`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The claim does not exist, belongs to another employee, cannot be cancelled in its current state, or the request is unauthenticated.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 404, 403, 409, or 401 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client deletes `/api/parking/claims/{claimId}`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `DELETE /api/parking/claims/{claimId}`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `cancelParkingClaim` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `assignment`, `page`, and `pageSize` filters are supplied.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response roster page contains `id`, `page`, `pages`, and an `employees` list with contract roster fields matching the supplied filters.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/roster`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/roster`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/roster`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getParkingRoster` operation with documented search, assignment, pagination parameters, response schema, and status codes in `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `result`, and `page` filters are supplied.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response page contains `id`, `page`, `pages`, and a `checks` list with contract entry-check fields matching the supplied filters.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/entry-checks`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/entry-checks`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/entry-checks`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getEntranceChecks` operation with documented filters, response schema, and status codes in `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A car detection has a readable plate with active temporary parking authorization for the detected office date.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response reports the detected plate, `verificationResult` `Authorized`, `entryStatus`, and `indicatorCommand` `Green`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client posts the detection to `/api/entrance/verify`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The detection is a pedestrian, motorcycle, or other non-car object.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response has a null `plate`, `indicatorCommand` `None`, and the contract-defined non-car outcome fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client posts the detection to `/api/entrance/verify`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A car has no valid authorization, its plate is unreadable, or a required entrance service is unavailable.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response reports a denied or unsuccessful outcome with `indicatorCommand` `None`, and the response status is 200 for processed detections or 503 for the unavailable-service outcome.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client posts the detection to `/api/entrance/verify`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A detection has been processed, including a non-car or unsuccessful detection.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"A database row records the detection time, office date and time, plate where available, verification result, entry status, and detail, and the response `checks` list contains the corresponding record.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client posts the detection and an administrator later requests matching entry checks.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An entrance detection request is malformed.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/entrance/verify`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a client submits `POST /api/entrance/verify`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the unauthenticated `verifyEntranceDetection` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml` and record each verification outcome in App.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and an omitted or valid `weekStart` date are supplied and parking activity exists for the requested week.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response report contains `weekStart`, `weekEnd`, `generatedAt`, `releasedSpaces`, `temporaryClaims`, `overallUtilizationPercent`, `dailyStatistics`, and `unusedParking`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/utilization`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated, the caller is not an administrator, or `weekStart` is invalid.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401, 403, or 400 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/utilization`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/utilization`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getWeeklyUtilizationReport` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session exists and office parking settings are stored in App.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains `timezone`, `releaseTime`, `schedulingWindowDays`, `reportRecipients`, `nextReportDelivery`, and `reportSchedule` matching the stored settings.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/office-settings`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/office-settings`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/office-settings`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getOfficeParkingSettings` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and valid `timezone`, `releaseTime`, and non-empty `reportRecipients` are supplied.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the saved settings fields; a subsequent response from `GET /api/admin/office-settings` returns the saved values.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator updates `/api/admin/office-settings`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The update is invalid, unauthenticated, or sent by a non-administrator.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 401, or 403 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `PUT /api/admin/office-settings`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator submits `PUT /api/admin/office-settings`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `updateOfficeParkingSettings` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `eventType`, and `page` filters are supplied, and retained activity exists.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains `page`, `pages`, and an `activity` list containing matching records with the contract activity fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/activity`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/activity`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/activity`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getParkingActivity` operation and return the activity field as specified by the d1 reading.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `eventType`, and `page` filters are supplied, and retained activity exists.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-22.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains `id`, `page`, `pages`, and an `events` list containing matching records with the contract `ParkingActivity` fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/activity`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-22.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/activity`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/activity`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getParkingActivity` operation and return the events field as specified by the d2 and d3 readings.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid availability request has a positive `availableSpaces` value and the email service accepts dispatch for eligible non-dedicated employees.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-23.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 202 and the response dispatch contains request `id`, status `accepted`, `recipientCount`, and template `parking-availability`; an outbound call is recorded to the configured email delivery service for eligible recipients.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client posts to `/api/notifications/availability`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The availability request is invalid or the required email service is unavailable.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-23.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 503 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/notifications/availability`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a client submits `POST /api/notifications/availability`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the unauthenticated `sendAvailabilityNotification` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`, dispatching the fixed `parking-availability` template to eligible non-dedicated employees through a configured email service.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-23\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"`ConnectionStrings:App` points to a fresh PostgreSQL database.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"A row in PostgreSQL `information_schema.tables` identifies each created application table.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A fresh App database is configured and demo seeding is disabled.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The registration response status is 201, a corresponding row exists in the configured App database, and the later response `vehicles` list contains the saved record.\",\n     \"when\": \"An authenticated client registers a vehicle, the API restarts against the same database, and the employee lists vehicles.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 9,\n     \"lineStart\": 6,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"// PostgreSQL: the connection comes from ConnectionStrings__App and nowhere else. There is no built-in login: an app that is\\n// not given one stops when it first needs the database, so it can never run on a password that is written in the code.\\nbuilder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDb>(o => o.UseNpgsql(builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\\\"App\\\")\\n    ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\\\"No database connection is configured. Set ConnectionStrings__App (for example Host=...;Port=5432;Database=...;Username=...;Password=«SECRET_2»\")));\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 20,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\\n        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 7,\n     \"lineStart\": 5,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/AppDb.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"public class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\\n{\\n}\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall persist API-managed application records in the PostgreSQL database configured by `ConnectionStrings:App` and initialize its schema on startup using the existing fresh-database `EnsureCreated` behavior.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-24\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The App database schema exists, its application tables are empty, and `Seed:Demo` is true.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-25.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The row count is between two and five in every application table; each table has at least two schema-valid sample rows, including at least two in non-singleton tables and at least one valid row in any contract-defined singleton table, with contract examples where available such as Aisha Rahman's employee and Toyota Corolla vehicle.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts and invokes the public `SeedData.Run` method.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An empty database has its application tables created.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-25.2\",\n     \"level\": \"unit\",\n     \"then\": \"Rows are present in each application table and each seeded row is schema-valid.\",\n     \"when\": \"A test calls the public `SeedData.Run` method directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The App database schema exists and `Seed:Demo` is unset or false.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-25.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The row count of demo-only sample records remains zero.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts and initializes its database.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 10,\n     \"lineStart\": 3,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/SeedData.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"// Sample rows for a person trying the product. The app calls Run at startup, after the tables exist, only when the setting\\n// Seed:Demo is true (the factory's run files set it; tests never do). Add rows to a table only when that table is empty.\\npublic static class SeedData\\n{\\n    public static void Run(AppDb db)\\n    {\\n    }\\n}\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 20,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\\n        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 86,\n     \"lineStart\": 72,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"              example:\\n                id: 101\\n                employeeId: \\\"F3-1042\\\"\\n                employeeName: \\\"Aisha Rahman\\\"\\n                corporateEmail: \\\"aisha.rahman@folio3.com\\\"\\n                dedicatedParking: true\\n                assignedFloor: \\\"B2\\\"\\n                assignedSpace: \\\"B2-114\\\"\\n                vehicles:\\n                  - id: 501\\n                    plate: \\\"KLG-4821\\\"\\n                    make: \\\"Toyota\\\"\\n                    model: \\\"Corolla\\\"\\n                    color: \\\"Silver\\\"\\n                    active: true\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When `Seed:Demo` is true, the Folio3 Parking API shall use `App.Api/SeedData.cs` to insert schema-valid sample rows into every empty application table, using contract example values where available and plausible values otherwise.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-25\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"ASM-2\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A fresh App database has `Seed:Demo` false and explicitly provisioned identities as needed.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-26.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response statuses and returned values are determined by test-created records, the suite completes without requiring any demo-seed row, and any empty roster response has count 0.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API test suite runs contract scenarios, arranging the records each scenario requires through setup or API calls.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 23,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 17,\n     \"lineStart\": 12,\n     \"path\": \"App.Tests/HealthTests.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"    [Fact]\\n    public async Task ApiIsUp()\\n    {\\n        var res = await _factory.CreateClient().GetAsync(\\\"/\\\");\\n        Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.OK, res.StatusCode);\\n    }\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API and its contract test suite shall serve documented operations and run test scenarios using explicitly arranged records, without requiring demo-seed rows.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-26\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API deployment is available for inspection.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-27.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The API health response and API documentation may be displayed, but no employee, administrator, or security-guard product screen is shown.\",\n     \"when\": \"A reviewer visits the root route and API documentation and inspects the served pages and product routes.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API repository shall not add employee, administrator, or security-guard product screens; its product surfaces remain contracted HTTP operations and API documentation.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-27\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"decisions\" kind=\"decisions\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"This spec contains 27 requirements—about three runs’ worth of work. Should it be approved as one run, or should it be narrowed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve the full spec as one run.\",\n  \"settles\": [\n   \"L9 size: This spec has 27 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<untrusted_document id=\"request\" source=\"cli\">\nFolio3 Parking App\n\nIntroduction\n\nFolio3 has a fixed number of parking spaces available at its office premises, while the number of\nemployees commuting to the office by car is greater than the available parking capacity.\nDedicated parking spaces are currently assigned to employees based on defined organizational criteria,\nincluding seniority, designation, and other relevant factors. Employees with dedicated parking are issued\na vehicle sticker, allowing security personnel to identify vehicles that are authorized to enter and use the\noffice parking area.\n\nHowever, dedicated parking spaces often remain unused when the assigned employee is on leave,\nworking from home, travelling, or otherwise not visiting the office. At the same time, other employees\nwho commute by car may be required to park outside the office despite parking spaces being\ntemporarily available inside the premises.\n\nTo improve the utilization of available parking spaces, Folio3 plans to introduce a mobile application\nthrough which employees with dedicated parking can release their parking space when they do not\nintend to use it. The released spaces can then be made available to other eligible employees through a\ntransparent and controlled process.\n\nThe application will be available on both iOS and Android platforms.\n\nProblem Statement\n\nThe current parking allocation process does not provide visibility into whether an assigned\nparking space will be used on a particular day.\n\nAs a result:\n\n● Dedicated parking spaces may remain vacant for the entire day.\n● Employees without dedicated parking may have to park on nearby roads.\n● Security personnel do not have real-time information about released or temporarily\nreassigned parking spaces.\n● Parking availability is managed through informal communication or is not managed at all.\n● The organization is unable to measure parking demand, utilization, or recurring\navailability.\n\nA centralized parking management application is required to enable parking holders to release\nunused spaces and allow those spaces to be allocated temporarily to other employees.\n\nSolution Overview\n\nThe proposed solution will consist of a mobile application available for both iOS and Android,\nsupported by a centralized backend system and a camera-based vehicle verification system at\nthe office entrance.\n\nEmployees will log in using their Folio3 Google account (Gmail). The system will automatically\nidentify the employee and retrieve their profile information using their corporate email address.\n\nFor employees with dedicated parking, the system will already maintain information such as:\n\n● Employee ID\n● Employee Name\n● Assigned Parking Status\n● Registered Vehicle License Plate Number\n\nEmployees using the application for the first time who do not have a registered vehicle will be\nprompted to enter their vehicle's license plate number. This information will be stored for future\nparking requests.\n\nBy default, the system will assume that employees with dedicated parking will use their\nassigned parking space on each working day. If they do not intend to come to the office, they\ncan release their parking space through a single action in the mobile application for the current\nday or schedule future releases using a calendar for up to 30 days.\n\nOnce a parking space is released, it becomes available to employees without dedicated\nparking. Eligible employees will receive a push notification and can claim the available space on\na first-come, first-served basis.\n\nAt the office entrance, vehicles with permanent parking stickers will continue to follow the\nexisting process. Vehicles without stickers will be verified using a license plate recognition\ncamera. The system will validate the vehicle against the temporary parking allocation for that\nday and, if authorized, activate a green indicator for the security guard to allow entry.\n\nUser Roles\n\nDedicated Parking Holder\n\nAn employee with a permanently assigned parking space who can release their parking when it\nwill not be used.\n\nTemporary Parking User\n\nAn employee without a dedicated parking space who can claim an available parking spot on a\nfirst-come, first-served basis.\n\nSecurity Guard\n\nA security staff member responsible for verifying vehicle entry based on parking stickers or\nsystem authorization.\n\nParking Administrator\n\nAn authorized administrator responsible for managing parking assignments, employee records,\nsystem configuration, and parking reports.\n\nUser Stories\n\nUS-001: Login with Folio3 Account\n\nUser Story\n\nAs an employee, I want to sign in using my Folio3 Google account so that I can securely access\nthe parking management application.\n\nDescription\n\nThe application shall support authentication using Folio3 Google Workspace accounts only.\nPersonal Gmail accounts or other email providers shall not be permitted.\n\nUpon successful login, the system shall identify the employee using their corporate email\naddress and retrieve their profile information.\n\nFor employees with dedicated parking, the system shall automatically import and maintain the\nfollowing information:\n\n● Employee ID\n● Employee Name\n● Assigned Parking Status\n● One or more registered vehicle license plate numbers\n● Assigned parking floor\n● Vehicle make\n● Vehicle model\n\n● Vehicle color\n\nEmployees without dedicated parking will be required to complete their vehicle profile during\ntheir first login by registering at least one license plate number. The remaining employee\ninformation shall be retrieved automatically from the corporate directory.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● Employee can log in using a Folio3 Google account.\n● Only authorized Folio3 employees can access the application.\n● Employees with dedicated parking have their profile populated automatically after login.\n● A dedicated parking holder may have one or more registered vehicles.\n● Employees without dedicated parking are prompted to register at least one vehicle\nduring their first login.\n● A vehicle profile includes the license plate number and optionally the vehicle make,\nmodel, and color.\n● Returning users are taken directly to the application dashboard after successful\nauthentication.\n\nS-002: Release Parking for Today\n\nUser Story\n\nAs an employee with a dedicated parking space, I want to release my parking for the current\nday with a single tap so that another employee can use it if I am not coming to the office.\n\nDescription\n\nEmployees with dedicated parking shall be able to release their assigned parking space for the\ncurrent day directly from the home screen.\n\nThe action should require a single tap (with an optional confirmation prompt) to make the\nprocess quick and convenient. Once the parking is released, the space shall immediately\nbecome available for temporary allocation to other eligible employees on a first-come,\nfirst-served basis.\n\nIf the parking space has already been claimed by another employee, the dedicated parking\nholder will no longer have access to that parking space for the remainder of the day.\n\nThe application shall clearly display the current status of the parking space (e.g., Reserved,\nReleased, or Claimed by Another Employee).\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● Only employees with dedicated parking can access this feature.\n● The option to \"Release Today's Parking\" is available on the home screen.\n● Releasing today's parking requires a single user action.\n● Once released, the parking space is immediately made available to eligible employees.\n● The parking status is updated in real time.\n● The user receives a confirmation that the parking has been released successfully.\n● The user cannot release the same parking space multiple times for the same day.\n● If the parking has already been claimed by another employee, the user is informed that\nthe parking cannot be reclaimed for that day without administrator intervention.\n\nUS-003: Schedule Future Parking Release\n\nUser Story\n\nAs an employee with a dedicated parking space, I want to schedule the release of my parking\nfor future dates so that my parking space can be utilized by others when I know I will not be\ncoming to the office.\n\nDescription\n\nThe application shall provide a calendar interface that allows dedicated parking holders to\nrelease their parking for future dates, up to 30 days in advance.\n\nUsers may select individual dates or multiple dates from the calendar. Once scheduled, the\nparking space will automatically become available for temporary allocation on the selected\ndates.\n\nThe user may cancel a scheduled parking release at any time, provided the parking space has\nnot already been claimed by another employee. If the parking has already been allocated, the\nrelease cannot be reverted without administrator intervention.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n● Only employees with dedicated parking can access this feature.\n● A calendar view is available to schedule future parking releases.\n● Users can release parking for any date within the next 30 days.\n● Users can select one or multiple dates.\n● Scheduled releases are saved and displayed on the calendar.\n● Users can cancel a scheduled release if the parking has not yet been claimed.\n● If the parking has already been claimed, the user is informed that the release cannot be\nreverted.\n● The system maintains an audit trail of all scheduled releases and cancellations.\n\nUS-004: Claim Available Parking\n\nUser Story\n\nAs an employee without a dedicated parking space, I want to claim an available parking spot so\nthat I can park inside the office premises when a space becomes available.\n\nDescription\n\nParking spaces shall be allocated on a first-come, first-served basis.\n\nParking spaces released in advance through the planning calendar shall become available for\nclaiming at the Daily Parking Release Time (default: 8:00 AM, configurable by the\nadministrator).\n\nIf a dedicated parking holder releases their parking on the same day:\n\n● If the release occurs before the Daily Parking Release Time, the parking space shall\nbecome available at the Daily Parking Release Time.\n● If the release occurs after the Daily Parking Release Time, the parking space shall\nbecome available immediately.\n\nWhenever one or more parking spaces become available, eligible employees without dedicated\nparking shall receive a push notification.\n\nThe application shall display the total number of available parking spaces (e.g., 5 Parking\nSpots Available). Employees will not select a specific parking space. Upon successfully\nclaiming a parking spot, the system shall automatically allocate one of the available parking\nspaces and inform the employee of the assigned parking floor.\n\nThe application will not validate whether the employee actually parks on the assigned floor.\nFloor allocation is intended only to distribute vehicles evenly across available parking areas.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● Only employees without dedicated parking can claim available parking.\n● Parking spaces are allocated on a first-come, first-served basis.\n● Pre-scheduled parking releases become available at the Daily Parking Release Time.\n● Same-day releases made before the Daily Parking Release Time become available at\nthe Daily Parking Release Time.\n● Same-day releases made after the Daily Parking Release Time become available\nimmediately.\n● Eligible employees receive a push notification when parking becomes available.\n● The application displays the number of currently available parking spaces.\n● A parking space can only be claimed once.\n\n● Upon a successful claim, the system automatically assigns a parking space and displays\nthe allocated parking floor.\n● The application records the date, time, employee, and assigned parking for audit\npurposes.\n● The application does not enforce or verify whether the employee parks on the assigned\nfloor.\n\nUS-005: Verify Vehicle at Parking Entrance\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a security guard, I want the system to automatically verify vehicles entering the parking area\nso that only authorized vehicles are allowed to enter.\n\nDescription\n\nThe parking entrance shall be equipped with a License Plate Recognition (LPR) camera and a\nstatus indicator light.\n\nThe camera shall continuously monitor approaching vehicles and identify their license plate\nnumbers. The system shall ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects.\n\nFor each detected vehicle, the system shall verify whether it has a valid parking authorization for\nthe current day.\n\nThe operational flow shall be as follows:\n\n● Vehicles displaying a permanent Folio3 parking sticker will continue to follow the existing\nprocess and will not be stopped by the security guard, even if the parking holder had\npreviously released their parking through the application.\n● Vehicles without a permanent parking sticker shall be stopped by the security guard.\n● The system shall verify the detected license plate against the temporary parking\nallocation for the current day.\n● If a valid parking authorization exists, the system shall activate the green indicator light.\n● Upon seeing the green light, the security guard shall allow the vehicle to enter.\n● If no valid authorization exists, the indicator light shall remain off and the vehicle shall not\nbe permitted to enter.\n\nAll successful and unsuccessful verification attempts shall be recorded for audit and reporting\npurposes.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● The camera detects approaching cars and reads their license plate numbers.\n● The system ignores pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects.\n\n● Vehicles with permanent parking stickers are not required to undergo system verification.\n● Vehicles without parking stickers are verified against the day's parking allocations.\n● The green indicator light is activated only when a valid parking authorization exists.\n● The indicator light remains off when no valid authorization is found.\n● The system records the date, time, license plate number, verification result, and entry\nstatus for every verification attempt.\n\nUS-006: Track Parking Utilization and Generate Weekly Reports\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a Parking Administrator, I want the system to track parking utilization and identify unused\nparking allocations so that management can monitor parking usage and improve utilization.\n\nDescription\n\nThe system shall use vehicle entry records captured through the License\nPlate Recognition (LPR) camera to determine whether allocated parking\nspaces were actually utilized.\n\nFor Phase 1, the system shall only monitor, record, and report parking\nutilization. No automated penalties or policy enforcement shall be applied.\n\nThe system shall track the following scenarios:\n\nScenario 1 – Dedicated Parking Not Utilized\n\n● The employee has a dedicated parking space.\n● The employee did not release their parking for the day.\n● The employee's registered vehicle was not detected entering the parking facility.\n● The parking shall be recorded as Unused Dedicated Parking.\n\nScenario 2 – Temporary Parking Not Utilized\n\n● The employee successfully claimed a temporary parking space.\n● The employee's registered vehicle was not detected entering the parking facility on that\nday.\n● The parking shall be recorded as Unused Temporary Parking.\n\nThe system shall maintain a history of these events for reporting and future policy\nimplementation.\n\nA weekly utilization report shall be generated automatically and emailed every Monday\nmorning to designated stakeholders.\n\nThe report should include, at a minimum:\n\n● Employees with dedicated parking who did not release or utilize their parking.\n● Employees who claimed temporary parking but did not utilize it.\n● Daily and weekly parking utilization statistics.\n● Total number of released parking spaces.\n● Total number of temporary parking claims.\n● Overall parking utilization percentage.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n● The system identifies unused dedicated parking based on the absence of a vehicle entry\nrecord.\n● The system identifies unused temporary parking based on the absence of a vehicle entry\nrecord.\n● All utilization events are stored with the corresponding employee, vehicle, and date.\n● A weekly parking utilization report is generated automatically every Monday morning.\n● The report is emailed to the configured stakeholders.\n● No automated warning, suspension, or penalty is applied in Phase 1.\n\nThis run builds the API side of the product above, in an existing .NET API project. Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there. Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads), and write its sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show. The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows. The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\n</untrusted_document>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-24 has an anchor that doesn't match the code\n</failures>\n\nEach decision answers a question about a problem in this spec. Change the spec so it does exactly what each answer says: add or change requirements and acceptance criteria, cite the answer id (Q-n) in \"sources\", and remove what an answer leaves out. Keep requirement IDs stable where the meaning doesn't change. Change nothing the decisions don't need. Never move requested behaviour out of scope or delete the requirements that cover an intent span.\nAnswer with the changes only, not the whole spec: \"requirements\" holds each requirement you change or add, whole, with all of its acceptance criteria; \"nfrs\" each NFR you change or add; \"removed\" the ids you delete; \"outOfScope\" and \"assumptions\" the whole list, only when it changes. Everything you leave out stays exactly as it is."}